  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Consider the d\u2019Alembert differential equation\n\n$$\ny=x(1+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})+\\frac{3}{2}{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nIf ${y}^{\u2032}(x)=t,$ then general solution can be expressed in parametric form $(x(t),y(t)),$ where\n\n$$\nx(t)=C{e}^{-t}+f(t)\n$$\n\nand $C$ is an arbitrary constant. Find the function $f(t).$\n\n*Hint: Under the given transformation, we have*\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+x=1-3t.\n$$\n\n*You may also wish to make use of the following result (constants omitted):*\n\n$$\n\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t=(t-1){e}^{t}\n$$",
